From: Yury Ilyanok <yury.ilyanok@gmail.com>
Subject: net: phy: realtek: add missing probe for RTL8226B/RTL8221B-CG

The RTL8226B-CG/RTL8221B-CG (0x001cc848) driver entry uses
rtl822xb_config_init, which dereferences the rtl822x_priv allocated by
rtl822x_probe (the ALDPS setup reads priv->enable_aldps), but the entry
lacks a .probe callback so phydev->priv stays NULL and the first
config_init oopses:

  Unable to handle kernel access to user memory ... at virtual address 0
  Call trace:
   rtl822x_set_serdes_option_mode
   phy_init_hw
   phy_attach_direct
   phylink_fwnode_phy_connect

Every other RTL822x entry that uses this config_init already has
.probe = rtl822x_probe; add it here too.

Signed-off-by: Yury Ilyanok <yury.ilyanok@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2376,6 +2376,7 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		PHY_ID_MATCH_EXACT(0x001cc848),
 		.name		= "RTL8226B-CG_RTL8221B-CG 2.5Gbps PHY",
 		.soft_reset	= genphy_soft_reset,
+		.probe		= rtl822x_probe,
 		.get_features	= rtl822x_get_features,
 		.config_aneg	= rtl822x_config_aneg,
 		.config_init	= rtl822xb_config_init,
